# tailnet-keeper renders the active physical and Tailscale interfaces.
#
# The bypass source is the bare interface name, not `(name)`. pf resolves
# `(name)` to the first address of each family only; macOS sends IPv6 from a
# temporary address that is never the first, so a v6 rule written that way
# matches nothing. The bare name expands to every address the interface holds
# at load time, and the keeper reloads the anchor whenever the addresses
# change. The tailnet rules keep `(name)`: utun4 holds exactly one address
# per family, and the parentheses let pf track it without a reload.
table <tailscale_derp> persist file "__DERP_IPV4_CACHE__"
table <tailscale_derp6> persist file "__DERP_IPV6_CACHE__"

pass out quick on __PHYSICAL_INTERFACE__ inet proto tcp from __PHYSICAL_INTERFACE__ to { 192.200.0.0/24, 199.165.136.0/24 } port { 80, 443 } keep state
pass out quick on __PHYSICAL_INTERFACE__ inet6 proto tcp from __PHYSICAL_INTERFACE__ to { 2606:b740:49::/48, 2606:b740:1::/48 } port { 80, 443 } keep state
pass out quick on __PHYSICAL_INTERFACE__ inet proto tcp from __PHYSICAL_INTERFACE__ to <tailscale_derp> port { 80, 443 } keep state
pass out quick on __PHYSICAL_INTERFACE__ inet proto udp from __PHYSICAL_INTERFACE__ to <tailscale_derp> port 3478 keep state
pass out quick on __PHYSICAL_INTERFACE__ inet6 proto tcp from __PHYSICAL_INTERFACE__ to <tailscale_derp6> port { 80, 443 } keep state
pass out quick on __PHYSICAL_INTERFACE__ inet6 proto udp from __PHYSICAL_INTERFACE__ to <tailscale_derp6> port 3478 keep state

pass out quick on __TAILSCALE_INTERFACE__ inet from (__TAILSCALE_INTERFACE__) to 100.64.0.0/10 no state
pass in quick on __TAILSCALE_INTERFACE__ inet from 100.64.0.0/10 to (__TAILSCALE_INTERFACE__) no state
pass out quick on __TAILSCALE_INTERFACE__ inet6 from (__TAILSCALE_INTERFACE__) to fd7a:115c:a1e0::/48 no state
pass in quick on __TAILSCALE_INTERFACE__ inet6 from fd7a:115c:a1e0::/48 to (__TAILSCALE_INTERFACE__) no state
